keywords:
  - fracture mechanics
  - continuum damage mechanics
  - crack-band regularization
  - finite element method
  - MATLAB
  - Abaqus
  - UMAT
abstract: >-
  FRACMATH is a MATLAB framework for finite element simulation of fracture in
  quasibrittle materials using scalar isotropic continuum damage mechanics,
  modified von Mises equivalent strain, exponential softening, and
  direction-dependent Oliver crack-band regularization.
  The SoftwareX study includes a hybrid 2D GPU backend with CPU sparse
  factorization, CPU/SMP size and mesh comparisons, and three timing observations for each computing configuration, and a
  three-mesh 3D pure-tension numerical mesh-consistency check.
  Mixed-mode and torsion examples are qualitative demonstrations.
